# Line endings are decided here, not by whatever editor or tool last wrote a file.
#
# Without this the repo carried 77 files permanently listed as modified: LF in
# git, CRLF on disk, and not one real content difference between them. That is
# worse than untidy. It hides genuine changes in noise and makes every diff and
# every blame argue with you.
#
# text=auto lets git decide per file whether it is text and store text as LF.
# eol=lf checks text out as LF as well, on Windows too, so the working tree
# matches what is stored and nothing drifts back the next time a file is saved.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, marked so git never inspects their bytes or tries to fix them.
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is text and its diffs are worth reading, so it stays text.
